{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed402918419/14/des.md && printf '\\\\n---PROMPT---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed402918419/14/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据封闭区域内部\"种子\"像素的颜色，从配色图例中查找对应的填充图案，将该图案平铺填满整个封闭区域。\n- `Input structure`：背景色为黑色。网格中有若干用同一种边框颜色（如 grey）绘制的封闭矩形区域，每个矩形区域内部恰好有一个非黑色、非边框色的单像素\"种子\"。网格的一个角落有一个独立的配色图例区：图例由若干行组成，每行左端一个颜色像素作为索引色，右侧紧跟一个小的 2×2 或 3×3 图案块（由多种颜色组成）。种子像素的颜色与图例索引色一一对应。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 识别图例区中的所有索引色与对应图案块。\n  2. 对每个封闭矩形，找到其内部的种子像素颜色，在图例中查找匹配的索引色。\n  3. 将该索引色对应的图案块以平铺方式填满矩形内部（从矩形内部左上角开始按行按列重复图案），种子像素被图案覆盖。\n  4. 边框像素保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：种子像素不是装饰，而是图例查找的关键——它将每个区域与一个特定的平铺图案绑定。解题者需要先识别角落的图例结构（索引色→图案映射），再将正确的图案铺入对应区域。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中散落的彩色碎片按颜色分组，每组碎片按其相对位置关系拼合成一个完整形状，然后将各完整形状按面积从大到小排列到输出网格中。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干种颜色的像素碎片（4-连通区域），同一颜色的碎片有多块，分散在网格各处。每种颜色的所有碎片恰好能无重叠地拼合成一个完整矩形（碎片之间的相对位移关系需要从它们在输入中的行列坐标差推断）。不同颜色拼合后的矩形大小不同。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 将所有碎片按颜色分组。\n  2. 对每种颜色，找到该颜色所有碎片像素的坐标集合，将它们的坐标统一平移使最小行列为 (0,0)，这些坐标形成该颜色的完整形状。\n  3. 计算每种颜色完整形状的像素数量（面积）。\n  4. 创建输出网格：将所有完整形状按面积从大到小、从上到下紧密排列（每个形状的左上角对齐网格左边界，相邻形状之间留一行黑色间隔）。\n- `Key insight`：碎片在输入中的绝对位置本身就编码了拼合信息——同色碎片之间的相对位移保持不变地\"焊接\"在一起。解题者需要发现碎片不是要移动到某个目标位置，而是要就地合并坐标，再按面积排序输出。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据每行中\"信号\"像素的数量，从该行的一端生长出等长的彩色条，生长方向由同行中一个箭头标记决定。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。每行包含零到多个散落的 green 像素（信号像素）和至多一个由三个相邻像素组成的箭头标记。箭头标记由 red 像素绘制：水平三像素成一排表示向右（红红红），或者竖直排列中间一个红像素与其左右各一个红像素构成\"T\"字——T 的横杠指向的方向即箭头方向（横杠在红竖线的右侧表示向右，在左侧表示向左）。具体地：箭头形态为一个 red 像素及其同行右侧紧邻的两个 red 像素（指向右）或左侧紧邻的两个 red 像素（指向左）。没有箭头的行保持不变。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 对每行，数出该行中 green 信号像素的数量 N。\n  2. 识别该行箭头标记的方向 D（向左或向右）。\n  3. 若 D 为向右，从该行最右边的信号像素的右邻位置起，向右连续填充 N 个 blue 像素（遇到网格边界则截断）。\n  4. 若 D 为向左，从该行最左边的信号像素的左邻位置起，向左连续填充 N 个 blue 像素（遇到网格边界则截断）。\n  5. 箭头标记的 red 像素和原有 green 像素保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：信号像素的\"数量\"决定生长条的长度，箭头标记决定生长方向和起点——两层信息来源不同但共同决定输出。解题者必须同时归纳出计数规则和方向规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在由分隔线划分的网格区域中，每个区域包含一个不完整的环形图案和一个颜色提示像素；根据提示像素的颜色在其他区域中找到形状匹配的完整环，然后将缺失部分补全，补全颜色取自提示像素。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。Azure 色的完整行和完整列将网格划分为若干等大的矩形区域。每个区域内有一个由某种颜色绘制的环形图案（闭合的单像素宽矩形环或 L 形环等），但其中一些区域的环缺失了一条边或一个角。每个缺失环的区域内还有一个孤立的单像素提示点，其颜色与某个其他区域中完整环的颜色相同。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 识别所有区域，将区域分为\"完整环区域\"（环没有缺口）和\"缺失环区域\"（环有缺口且含提示像素）。\n  2. 对每个缺失环区域，找到提示像素的颜色 C。\n  3. 在完整环区域中找到颜色为 C 的那个环，该环的形状就是目标形状。\n  4. 将缺失环区域的环补全为与目标环完全相同的形状，补全部分使用提示像素的颜色 C 绘制。\n  5. 提示像素本身从输出中移除。分隔线保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：提示像素的颜色是跨区域的索引——它指向另一个区域中的完整环作为\"模板\"。解题者需先通过颜色匹配建立区域间的对应关系，再利用完整模板推断缺失部分的位置和形状。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中的多色路径按照路径交叉点处的叠压关系分层，高层路径保留原色，低层路径在交叉点处被高层颜色覆盖。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干条单像素宽的直线路径（水平或垂直），每条路径用一种独特的非黑色颜色绘制。路径之间存在交叉点（两条路径共享一个像素位置）。在输入中，每个交叉点显示的是某一条路径的颜色（即\"上层\"路径的颜色）。网格的底部有一行颜色序列作为\"层级图例\"：从左到右排列若干颜色像素，左边的颜色层级最低（最先绘制，容易被覆盖），右边的颜色层级最高（最后绘制，覆盖他色）。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 读取底部层级图例，确定颜色的优先级排序（左低右高）。\n  2. 识别网格中所有路径及其颜色。\n  3. 对于每个交叉点（两条不同颜色路径交汇的位置），将该位置的像素设为层级更高的那种颜色。\n  4. 非交叉点的路径像素保持原色不变。层级图例行在输出中移除。\n- `Key insight`：输入中交叉点的颜色可能是对的也可能是错的——解题者不能直接信任输入中的交叉点颜色，必须先从图例中推断出层级关系，再据此\"重新仲裁\"每个交叉点的颜色归属。图例是解题的第一层推理，交叉覆盖是第二层。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：每个前景对象充当\"邮票\"，其盖章位置由对象内部嵌入的方向标记决定：将对象沿标记方向平移复制，直到与另一个对象或网格边缘接触，同时在原始位置只保留方向标记像素。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干个彩色的 4-连通对象，每个对象由一种主色和恰好一个不同颜色的单像素\"方向标记\"组成。方向标记在对象内部的位置编码了移动方向：标记位于对象最上方的像素行→向上移动；位于最下方→向下；位于最左列→向左；位于最右列→向右。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 对每个对象，找到其内部方向标记像素的位置，确定标记在对象边界框中的边（上/下/左/右）。\n  2. 将整个对象（包括标记像素）沿该方向逐步平移，直到对象的前沿碰到网格边界或另一个已定位对象的像素。\n  3. 在新位置绘制完整的对象（保持原色和形状）。\n  4. 在原始位置，仅保留方向标记像素（主色像素全部擦除为背景）。\n- `Key insight`：方向标记不仅指示移动方向，还在原位留下\"痕迹\"，形成一种\"发射-落点\"的视觉关系。解题者需要先识别标记在对象中的相对位置来推断方向（而非标记的颜色），再模拟碰撞停止。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格视为一幅\"拼图草稿\"，其中每个彩色区域边缘有若干缺口像素；通过匹配相邻区域的互补缺口形状，将缺口像素填充为正确的区域颜色。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格被划分为若干个相邻的单色矩形区域（非黑色），区域之间无间隙地紧密排列。每个区域的矩形边界上有若干像素被设为黑色（形成\"缺口\"），这些缺口像素总是成对出现在两个相邻区域的共享边上——一个区域的缺口位置恰好对应相邻区域的缺口位置（互补拼图齿）。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 识别所有矩形区域及其颜色。\n  2. 对于每个黑色缺口像素，确定它属于哪个区域（根据其在哪个矩形的边界范围内）。\n  3. 将每个缺口像素填充为其所属区域的颜色，恢复完整的矩形。\n- `Key insight`：黑色缺口像素看似背景，实则是矩形边界的\"损坏\"——解题者需要识别出这些黑色像素是区域的一部分而非真正的背景。关键在于发现每个缺口都可以通过其周围像素的颜色分布判断归属：缺口像素三面或两面被同色像素包围，那个颜色就是它的正确颜色。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：网格中散布着若干\"发射器\"和\"反射镜\"；从每个发射器射出一束光线，光线遇到反射镜时改变方向，光线经过的所有像素被染成发射器的颜色。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干个 2×2 的彩色方块作为\"发射器\"，每个发射器颜色不同。每个发射器恰好有一个边上紧邻一个 grey 单像素，该像素的位置决定光线的初始发射方向（grey 像素在发射器的上方→光线向上射出；在下方→向下；在左方→向左；在右方→向右）。网格中还散布着若干由两个相邻 maroon 像素组成的\"反射镜\"：水平排列的两个 maroon 像素构成水平反射镜（将垂直光线转为水平）；垂直排列的两个 maroon 像素构成垂直反射镜（将水平光线转为垂直）。反射方向遵循：光线从上或下碰到水平反射镜，转向右；光线从左或右碰到垂直反射镜，转向下。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 对每个发射器，确定初始发射方向（由紧邻的 grey 像素位置决定）。\n  2. 沿发射方向逐像素前进，将路径上的黑色像素染成发射器颜色。\n  3. 若光线碰到反射镜，按上述反射规则改变方向，继续前进。\n  4. 光线遇到网格边界或另一个发射器时停止。\n  5. 反射镜和发射器本身保持原色不变，grey 方向标记保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：解题的第一层是识别 grey 像素与发射器的空间关系以推断发射方向；第二层是理解 maroon 反射镜的朝向如何决定光线转弯规则。两层规则叠加后，光线路径形成非直觉的折线。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n---PROMPT---\n你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"7e4d4f7c\" lines=\"9-24\">\n<description>\nCompress the L-shaped cue to three rows and add a pink copy of the top-row foreground mask.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background color, a two-color top row, and all\nforeground pixels below the top row lie in the first column as vertical markers.\n\nRule\nKeep the input top row as output row 0 and the first marker row as output row 1.\nOutput row 2 is background except at the top-row foreground columns, which are\nrecolored pink.\n\nKey insight\nThe lower repeated marker rows only identify the vertical cue; the generated\nrow is a recolored mask of the horizontal cue in the top row.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"581f7754\" lines=\"8-22\">\n<description>\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \"marker\" pixel.\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\n\nRule:\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\n\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e734a0e8\" lines=\"44-59\">\n<description>\nCopy the unique colored sprite tile into every tiled cell marked by an internal separator-colored pixel.\n\nInput structure\n- Full same-color separator rows and columns partition the grid into equal rectangular tiles.\n- One tile contains the only non-background, non-separator colored sprite.\n- Target tiles are otherwise background-colored but contain at least one internal pixel of the separator color.\n\nRule\n- Keep the separator lines and the source sprite tile unchanged.\n- Replace each marked target tile with an exact copy of the source tile.\n- Unmarked background-only tiles remain unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The internal separator-colored pixels are placement markers; the single colored tile is the template to stamp into those marked cells.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"35ab12c3\" lines=\"73-88\">\n<description>\nComplete outlined shapes and carry attached shadow pixels along their edges.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. Each active color marks vertices of an 8-direction aligned outline.\n- A start vertex can have adjacent non-bg, different-colored shadow pixels.\n- Other colored pixels may be distractors unless they lie on valid drawable edges.\n\nRule:\n- For each color, order its pixels by polar angle around their centroid to form a cycle.\n- Draw only horizontal, vertical, or 45-degree edges whose interiors are clear.\n- From the chosen start vertex, copy adjacent shadow offsets along each drawable edge\n  when the parallel path is in bounds and clear.\n\nKey insight: The main outline is reconstructed first, then the start vertex's neighbor offsets define parallel shadow strokes.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"522fdd07\" lines=\"8-23\">\n<description>\nCycle each solid odd-sided square to the next smaller centered square, wrapping a single pixel to a 9x9 square.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has one dominant background color.\n- Every foreground object is a separated 4-connected monochrome solid square.\n- Square side lengths are odd and belong to the cycle 1, 3, 5, 7, 9.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the canvas to the background.\n- Keep each square's color and center.\n- Replace side length n by n - 2 when n > 1; replace side length 1 by side length 9.\n\nKey insight:\n- The visible operation is on square size, not color: side lengths cycle 1 -> 9 -> 7 -> 5 -> 3 -> 1.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5623160b\" lines=\"44-59\">\n<description>\nPush every colored object touching maroon markers straight outward until it reaches the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Maroon pixels are fixed markers.\n- Every other foreground 4-connected object touches the marker pixels on exactly one cardinal side.\n\nRule:\n- Clear each non-background, non-maroon object from its original position.\n- Translate it in the direction away from its maroon contact until the object reaches the grid boundary.\n- Keep the maroon marker pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The maroon contact side is a launcher: it determines a unique outward ray for the whole object, and the edge of the grid determines the translation distance.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3cd86f4f\" lines=\"6-18\">\n<description>\nShear the rectangular input down-left onto a black canvas.\n\nInput structure\nA rectangular grid of colored pixels with no internal empty region to infer.\n\nRule\nCreate a black output with the same height and width W + H - 1, then copy\neach input row r unchanged starting at column H - 1 - r.\n\nKey insight\nThe colors and row contents are preserved; only the row offsets change so\nthe left edge forms a descending diagonal.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d255d7a7\" lines=\"99-114\">\n<description>\nMove the patterned edge band to the opposite edge along every row or column whose band slice contains the trail color.\n\nInput structure\n- The dominant color is the background.\n- The two foreground colors are a frequent trail color and a rarer marker color.\n- All marker pixels lie nearest to one grid edge, and that edge contains trail-color runs that define the source-band thickness.\n\nRule\n- Choose the source edge identified by the marker pixels.\n- A row or column perpendicular to that edge moves if its source-band slice contains the trail color.\n- Copy that slice unchanged to the opposite edge, erase the remaining trail cells to background, and keep marker-only lines fixed.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker color identifies the active edge, while the trail color identifies which parallel rows or columns carry an edge-band slice across the grid.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dfadab01\" lines=\"79-93\">\n<description>\nExpand each colored control pixel into its corresponding fixed 4x4 glyph.\n\nInput structure:\n- Black background with single-pixel markers in colors 2, 3, 5, and/or 8.\n- Some inputs also show a sample 4x4 glyph in the output color, with a same-rule marker just below-right of the sample.\n\nRule:\n- Replace each marker color by its learned 4x4 glyph: 2->yellow frame, 3->blue ring, 5->pink diagonal blocks, 8->orange X.\n- Paint each glyph with its top-left corner at the marker pixel, clipping at the grid boundary.\n- Remove the sample glyphs and skip their below-right label markers.\n\nKey insight:\n- The colored pixels are control pixels for a fixed glyph alphabet; non-control sample glyphs are only legend entries, not preserved scene objects.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"5545f144\" lines=\"191-207\">\n<description>\nMove a triangular sprite across the grid, consuming aligned marker pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- Frames concatenated horizontally with solid divider columns; bg is most common color.\n- Each frame: a triangular arrow-shaped sprite and scattered single-pixel markers, all one color.\n\nRule:\n- Start from the rightmost frame.\n- At each step, exactly one cardinal direction from the head has reachable\n  markers (on a half-line: same row or column); the sprite advances to the\n  nearest one.\n- On reaching a marker, consume it; sprite re-faces that direction.\n- Repeat until no markers remain; output the final sprite position on a clean bg.\n\nKey insight: The triangle's tip encodes facing direction, which sets marker-consumption priority.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"973e499e\" lines=\"7-22\">\n<description>\nExpand each input pixel into a miniature same-color mask of the whole grid.\n\nInput structure\n- The input is a non-empty two-dimensional grid of foreground colors.\n- Black is reserved for the empty/background pixels introduced in the expanded output.\n- The output has one input-shaped block for each input pixel.\n\nRule\n- For every input pixel with color c, replace that pixel by a block the same shape as the input.\n- Inside the block, write c exactly where the original input also has color c.\n- Write black everywhere else in the block.\n\nKey insight\nEach pixel selects the global mask of its own color; the result is the blockwise self-mask of the grid.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"668eec9a\" lines=\"29-47\">\n<description>\nSummarize the foreground line objects as ordered horizontal color stripes.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background fills a rectangular grid.\n- Each non-background color forms one contiguous one-cell-thick line segment.\n- The line segments have distinct topmost rows, and there are at most five of\n  them.\n\nRule:\n- Sort the foreground colors by the topmost row occupied by their line\n  segment.\n- Create a 5x3 output filled with the background color.\n- Place one solid 1x3 row for each foreground color, preserving that\n  top-to-bottom order and padding any unused rows above with background.\n\nKey insight: The exact line length and slope do not matter; only the\nvertical order of the colored line segments is encoded in the output stack.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"60d73be6\" lines=\"22-39\">\n<description>\nComplete the sparse colored marker pattern by reflecting it across a full-row/full-column cross.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background and one non-background cross color that\nfills exactly one complete row and one complete column. All other foreground\npixels are sparse markers away from that cross.\n\nRule\nKeep the input unchanged, and for each marker pixel copy its color to the\npositions obtained by reflecting it across the cross row, across the cross\ncolumn, and across both axes. Reflected positions outside the grid are\nclipped.\n\nKey insight\nThe full cross is not a copied object; it is the pair of mirror axes for\ncompleting the quadrant pattern.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"4a1cacc2\" lines=\"8-23\">\n<description>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
